#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.backend"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:6
msgid ""
"Default backend to use for rebasing.  Possible choices are 'apply' or "
"'merge'.  In the future, if the merge backend gains all remaining "
"capabilities of the apply backend, this setting may become unused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.stat"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:10
msgid ""
"Whether to show a diffstat of what changed upstream since the last "
"rebase. False by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.autoSquash"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:15
msgid ""
"If set to true, enable the `--autosquash` option of linkgit:git-rebase[1] by "
"default for interactive mode.  This can be overridden with the "
"`--no-autosquash` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.autoStash"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:25
msgid ""
"When set to true, automatically create a temporary stash entry before the "
"operation begins, and apply it after the operation ends.  This means that "
"you can run rebase on a dirty worktree.  However, use with care: the final "
"stash application after a successful rebase might result in non-trivial "
"conflicts.  This option can be overridden by the `--no-autostash` and "
"`--autostash` options of linkgit:git-rebase[1].  Defaults to false."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.updateRefs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:28
msgid "If set to true enable `--update-refs` option by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.missingCommitsCheck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:39
msgid ""
"If set to \"warn\", git rebase -i will print a warning if some commits are "
"removed (e.g. a line was deleted), however the rebase will still proceed. If "
"set to \"error\", it will print the previous warning and stop the rebase, "
"'git rebase --edit-todo' can then be used to correct the error. If set to "
"\"ignore\", no checking is done.  To drop a commit without warning or error, "
"use the `drop` command in the todo list.  Defaults to \"ignore\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.instructionFormat"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:44
msgid ""
"A format string, as specified in linkgit:git-log[1], to be used for the todo "
"list during an interactive rebase.  The format will automatically have the "
"commit hash prepended to the format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.abbreviateCommands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:48
msgid ""
"If set to true, `git rebase` will use abbreviated command names in the todo "
"list resulting in something like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tp deadbee The oneline of the commit\n"
"\tp fa1afe1 The oneline of the next commit\n"
"\t...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:56
msgid "instead of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tpick deadbee The oneline of the commit\n"
"\tpick fa1afe1 The oneline of the next commit\n"
"\t...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:64
msgid "Defaults to false."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.rescheduleFailedExec"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:69
msgid ""
"Automatically reschedule `exec` commands that failed. This only makes sense "
"in interactive mode (or when an `--exec` option was provided).  This is the "
"same as specifying the `--reschedule-failed-exec` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.forkPoint"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:72
msgid "If set to false set `--no-fork-point` option by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.rebaseMerges"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:82
msgid ""
"Whether and how to set the `--rebase-merges` option by default. Can be "
"`rebase-cousins`, `no-rebase-cousins`, or a boolean. Setting to true or to "
"`no-rebase-cousins` is equivalent to `--rebase-merges=no-rebase-cousins`, "
"setting to `rebase-cousins` is equivalent to "
"`--rebase-merges=rebase-cousins`, and setting to false is equivalent to "
"`--no-rebase-merges`. Passing `--rebase-merges` on the command line, with or "
"without an argument, overrides any `rebase.rebaseMerges` configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "rebase.maxLabelLength"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/rebase.txt:87
msgid ""
"When generating label names from commit subjects, truncate the names to this "
"length. By default, the names are truncated to a little less than `NAME_MAX` "
"(to allow e.g. `.lock` files to be written for the corresponding loose "
"refs)."
msgstr ""
